Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Keeps VirtualDJ's full-screen mode on the screen it was already on,
; instead of jumping to the external TV -- WITHOUT costing us the TV as a
; usable monitor.
;
; The window control in the header cycles windowed -> maximized ->
; full screen. On the last step VirtualDJ does everything right: it calls
; MonitorFromWindow, gets the laptop panel, and asks for that monitor's
; rect. Wine also does the right thing -- it sets _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN
; and then names the target output for the WM in _NET_WM_FULLSCREEN_MONITORS,
; using Xinerama monitor indices (0 = eDP-1, the laptop).
;
; mutter is what gets it wrong. meta_x11_display_ensure_xinerama_indices()
; matches XineramaQueryScreens() rects against its own logical monitor
; rects by *exact equality*. Both screens here run at scale 2, so mutter's
; logical rects (eDP-1 0,0 1920x1200; HDMI-2 1920,0 2048x1080) can never
; equal XWayland's device-pixel Xinerama rects (0,0 3840x2400 and
; 3840,0 4096x2160). No logical monitor is ever assigned an index, so they
; all keep the g_new0 default of 0. This is an upstream mutter bug, still
; present in main; it needs both HiDPI scaling and two monitors to show up.
;
; What that leaves is entirely decided by LIST ORDER, because
; meta_x11_display_xinerama_index_to_logical_monitor() returns the *first*
; logical monitor whose xinerama_index matches:
;   - index 0 (what Wine sends for the laptop) -> the first logical monitor
;     in mutter's list.
;   - index 1 (what Wine sends for the TV)     -> matches nothing, so mutter
;     calls meta_window_clear_fullscreen_monitors() and falls back to placing
;     the window by its real geometry -- which is already the TV. Correct by
;     accident, and why the visualisation window works either way.
;
; So the mitigation is not a Wine setting at all: put eDP-1's
; <logicalmonitor> FIRST in ~/.config/monitors.xml, and mutter's bogus
; index 0 resolves to the laptop, which is exactly what Wine asked for.
; Not managed declaratively -- GNOME owns that file and rewrites it whenever
; display settings are applied, so if full screen starts jumping to the TV
; again, check the order in monitors.xml first.
;
; DO NOT bring back "UseXRandR"="N" here (this file used to set it).
; It does stop the jumping, but only because it makes Wine blind to the TV:
; X11DRV_XRandR_Init() bails out, Wine keeps the "Xinerama" display-device
; handler, and display *settings* fall back to NoRes/XF86VidMode -- both of
; which only report a mode for the PRIMARY adapter. Modern Wine derives each
; monitor's rect from its source's current mode, so the TV's source gets
; mode 0x0 and therefore an empty rect. Measured 2026-09-10 with a
; Win32 probe in this prefix vs. a clean control prefix:
;
;                        UseXRandR=N      XRandR on
;   SM_CMONITORS              1               2
;   virtual screen      3840x2400        7936x2400
;   \\.\DISPLAY2 mode      0x0 @ 0,0   4096x2160 @ 3840,0
;
; With that set, VirtualDJ's monitor list holds a single "Generic Non-PnP
; Monitor" and the visualisation window can never be sent to the TV.
; Hotplug detection and mode setting are lost too, but losing the second
; monitor outright is the one that bites.
;
; Do NOT try to fix this by switching Wine to winewayland.drv
; (HKCU\Software\Wine\Drivers "Graphics"="wayland"). It does remove the
; faulty path -- the Wayland driver names outputs by connector, so there is
; no index to mistranslate -- and the UI renders at the correct size, but
; VirtualDJ livelocks within a minute: the main thread keeps wined3d's
; command-stream critical section while mutter re-sends
; xdg_toplevel_handle_configure with climbing serials, and the UI stops
; responding at ~80% CPU ("wait timed out in thread NNNN, blocked by NNNN"
; against dlls/wined3d/wined3d_main.c: wined3d_cs). Tested 2026-09-09 on
; wine 11.17.
;
; The import below actively DELETES the old value. A .reg import never
; removes what an earlier one wrote, so simply dropping the line would have
; left "UseXRandR"="N" in place in every existing prefix.
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\X11 Driver]
"UseXRandR"=-
